    "quote": "For all $\\delta$-correct algorithms, for all $\\theta\\in \\cM$, \\liminf_{\\delta\\to 0}\\frac{\\E_\\theta[\\tau_{\\delta}]}{\\log(1/\\delta)} \\geq \\Tstar(\\theta), where ... \\Tstar(\\theta)^{-1} \\eqdef \\max_{w \\in \\Sigma_A} \\inf_{\\lambda\\in \\neg \\istar(\\theta)} \\frac{1}{2}\\normm{\\theta - \\lambda}_{V_w}^2."
   },
   "confidence": "medium",
   "notes": "T_star is the linear characteristic time max_w inf_{lambda in alt} ||theta-lambda||^2_{V_w}/2 inverted. Paper notes this was already proved by Soare et al. 2014 for BAI; extension to general pure exploration. Proof also gives the non-asymptotic E[tau] >= T_star log(1/(2.4 delta))."
  },
